%[text] ### Introduction
%[text] This analysis injects low power targets into real collected HDTV data by attenuating, delaying, and doppler shifting the reference channel and adding it to the surveillance channel. Attenuation is done using the signal power in the surveillance channel as a reference.
%[text] We can roughly assume that the surveillance channel signal power is the direct path power and inject attenuated targets to measure our signal processing pipeline's ability to detect targets at different power levels using the direct path power as a reference.
%[text] So if we estimate that targets at the max range of interest would be 50 dB lower than the direct path, we can inject signals 50 dB lower than the surveillance channel signal power and see how good we are at detecting those targets.
%[text] We can perform range-Doppler processing and measure the SNR of the processed data. If the desired output is 90% Pd and 1e-6 FAR, the required SNR is ~13 dB:
pd = 0.9;
far = 1e-6;
requiredSnr = shnidman(pd, far);
disp(['Required SNR: ', num2str(requiredSnr)]) %[output:7c24abfd]
%[text] So we need a signal processing approach that will give us 13 dB SNR at the required attenuation level.
%[text] This approach may give us over-confidence because we are assuming the reference channel is a perfect estimate of the true direct path signal, I don't know how much extra SNR that gives us over reality.
%%
%[text] ### Test File Definition
%[text] Define the file that contains the captured reference and surveillance channels.
fname = 'n320_hdtv_capture_20260708T135521_part1';
%%
%[text] ### No Filter Test
%[text] Test the SNR results when no DSI suppression filter is used
signalProcessingNoFilter(fname,requiredSnr); %[output:796ea557]
%%
%[text] ### Baseline Processing Test
%[text] The baseline signal processing approach is a Wiener filter + RangeDoppler analysis rearranging data into a cube.
baselineSignalProcessingTest(fname,requiredSnr); %[output:4838f86b]
%%
%[text] ### Wiener Tap Variation Test
%[text] Test how the number of taps affects SNR.
wienerTapVariationTest(fname,requiredSnr); %[output:1c4212b8]
%%
%[text] ### BLMS Test
%[text] Test DSI suppression using BLMS.
%[text] Block least mean square DSI suppression.
blmsDsiSuppressionTest(fname,requiredSnr); %[output:29ae899b]
%%
%[text] ### ECA-CD Test
%[text] Test DSI suppression using ECA-CD.
ecaCdDsiSuppressionTest(fname,requiredSnr); %[output:3ec24012]
%%
%[text] ### Doppler Filter Bank Test
%[text] Test processing if we use a Doppler filter bank instead of rearranging into a data cube.
dopplerFilterBankTest(fname, requiredSnr); %[output:06633559]

